    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Bloodsports is the sixth studio album by Suede and marked their return after an 11-year gap following A New Morning. Released in 2013 on Warner Bros. Records, it finds the band leaning back into the dramatic, melodic, guitar-driven sound that defined their classic era, with Brett Anderson framing the record around the “endless carnal game of love.”\n\nThe album was widely heard as a reinvigoration of Suede’s style, with reviews praising its polished, forceful production and the return of Richard Oakes’s expressive guitar work and Anderson’s theatrical delivery. Songs such as “It Starts and Ends With You,” “For the Strangers,” and “Sabotage” reflect the album’s themes of lust, pursuit, and romantic collapse, giving Bloodsports a dark but energetic emotional arc that many critics saw as a strong comeback statement.",
